  "output": "Spec ID: token-efficient-tool-responses-ticket01-spec\nRevision: r40 (document: r40-replacement)\nFindings by ID: none\n\nNo unresolved HIGH/MEDIUM finding identified.\n\n**C7 verified closed — spec §4 AC38/43; §5 T2/T3.**\nEach AC38 assertion has a T2 executable boundary in `internal/service/result_handle.go` and `result_handle_test.go`:\n- Saturated aggregate, release-funded tombstone and exact nonpositive delta: retirement commit.\n- Empty retirement, zero delta and no residual records: store retirement.\n- No deferred work or subsequent charge movement: T2’s sweep hook.\n- Failed pre-commit owner resolution, no handle/entry/persistence, including after tombstone clearing: store commit and injected clock.\n\nThe session/SDK wording describes the production counterpart; T2’s observable is failed owner resolution, not inbound-map deletion.\n\nAC43/T3 separately requires admitted execution → production-trigger retirement → resumed over-ceiling result, without fixture-injected retirement. Its artifacts are `bounded_delivery.go`, the delivery/retrieval tests and `inbound.go`. `TestRetirementAdmissionUnconditional` and `TestInboundRetirementHooks` are distinct obligations; neither task’s PASS discharges the other.\n\n**C6 preserved:** R6/R7/R10 prohibit resurrection after empty retirement or tombstone clearing. Tombstone presence cannot substitute for current owner resolution. Existing retirement transactions independently checked at `projection.go:863–902` and `inbound.go:799–813,950–966,1120–1165`.\n\nThe prior LOW ledger advisory is only partially closed: §3 r35-C1’s affected-clauses cell still names the obsolete refusal-bookkeeping subtest. This historical pointer does not weaken a current oracle.\n\n**Per-requirement verdicts — cheap false pass → rejecting criterion**\n\n| R | Verdict | False pass → oracle |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 | PASS | Early paging/changed bytes → AC1/40 boundary goldens |\n| R2 | PASS | Measure payload only → AC2 duplicate-bearing literals |\n| R3 | PASS | Tiny prefix/unwired surface → AC3/19 |\n| R4 | PASS | Guessable/shared handles → crypto/rand inspection; AC4/16 |\n| R5 | PASS | Broken cuts/dead handles → AC6/17/19/37 reconstruction |\n| R6 | PASS | Uncharged containers/cross-owner eviction → AC7/15/36/38 |\n| R7 | PASS | Fixture-only retirement → AC8/38/43 |\n| R8 | PASS | Re-execute deterministic upstream → AC6/19 invocation counts |\n| R9 | PASS | Reload changes existing records → AC10/29 |\n| R10 | PASS | Generic terminal/empty prefix → AC11/26 isolated causes |\n| R11 | PASS | Accept infeasible config → T1 relation/headroom tests |\n| R12 | PASS | Dead registry/unsafe emission → AC13/14/44 |\n| R13 | PASS | Schema-only validation/wrong precedence → AC24/25/32 |\n| R14 | PASS | Truncation disguised as success → AC26 |\n| R15 | PASS | Unqualified completeness promise → AC27 |\n| R16 | PASS | Sweep-dependent codes/cap corruption → AC5/18/39 |\n\n8192 passes; 8193 pages. Bounds count escaped serialized `CallToolResult`, including blocks/metadata, excluding JSON-RPC framing. Page indices start at 1; totals/remainders count original serialized bytes, not runes; `is_error` remains preserved.\n\nT1–T5 each retain falsifiable checks. §7 binds emission/scraping to AC13/14; collector delivery remains the documented deployment-owned exception. No silent owner-decision resolution found; OD1–OD3 remain explicit defaults.\n\nLimits: full candidate read; no files changed or tests run. Hashes could not be independently recomputed. Binary-only observation cannot prove no-remarshal mechanics, entropy provenance, structural reclamation, registry completeness or documentation correctness. PASS is technical, not execution permission.\n\n### Verdict\nPASS\n",
